THE CLAIM UNDER TEST
  `spoolSuppressedKey` (packages/collector-cli/src/hook-spool.ts) reads:

      if (derivationInputKeys.has(key)) return false;
      if (spoolKeepsProtectedIdentityRaw(key)) return false;   <-- this line
      return collectorStripsKeyOutright(key);

  and `spoolKeepsProtectedIdentityRaw(key)` is
  `!collectorStripsKeyOutright(key) && isProtectedMetadataFieldName(key)`.
  The guard line can only fire where `collectorStripsKeyOutright(key)` is
  already false, and the final return answers `false` for exactly those keys.
  It decides nothing.

